0 ~Batima socket - the cup a stud enters
0 Name: batima-socket.dat
0 Author: spex project (geometry read off photographs of the real object)
0 !LDRAW_ORG Unofficial_Part
0 !LICENSE Licensed under CC BY 4.0 : see CAreadme.txt
0 // Origin at the block's BOTTOM face, LDraw +Y down, so the cup runs upward
0 // into the body from y = 0 to y = -7, then a narrower bore to y = -11.
0 //
0 // THE REAL SOCKET IS CONICAL - a countersunk cup - and this one is
0 // CYLINDRICAL. Stated because it is a real difference in how the joint
0 // works: a cone locates a block by sliding on a taper, a cylinder does not.
0 // Nothing in this piece ever sees the underside of a Batima block, so the
0 // cost today is zero and the debt is recorded rather than forgotten.
0 //
0 // A LESSON PAID FOR TWICE IN ONE SITTING: `4-4conN` and `4-4ringN` scale
0 // their RADII with the matrix, so `4-4ring3` scaled by 7 is not an annulus
0 // from 3 to 7 - it is one from 21 to 28, four times wider than the block,
0 // and it renders as a flat wing sticking out of the object. The radii here
0 // are therefore chosen to be expressible: the cup is 6 and its bore 2, so
0 // its floor is ring1 + ring2 at scale 2, spanning exactly 2 to 6.
0 //
0 // Inverted: these faces are seen from inside the cup.
0 BFC INVERTNEXT
1 16 0 -7 0 6 0 0 0 7 0 0 0 6 4-4cyli.dat
1 16 0 -7 0 2 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 2 4-4ring1.dat
1 16 0 -7 0 2 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 2 4-4ring2.dat
0 BFC INVERTNEXT
1 16 0 -11 0 2 0 0 0 4 0 0 0 2 4-4cyli.dat
1 16 0 -11 0 2 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 2 4-4disc.dat
1 16 0 0 0 6 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 6 4-4edge.dat
